cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite it using the metadata below.
title: >-
  Biomass Waste-to-Energy (WtE) Decision Framework: A Hybrid
  Clustering and Rule-Based Approach to Choose Thermochemical Conversion
  Technology.
authors:
  - given-names: Mishal
    family-names: Asmat
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Mishal-Asmat/biomass-wte-decision-framework'
abstract: >-
  A reproducible data-science pipeline that combines unsupervised
  fuel typology clustering (KMeans) with literature based
  thermochemical process-suitability rules to recommend the best possible
  waste-to-energy conversion technology (combustion,
  gasification, pyrolysis) for biomass and waste
  fuel samples. It includes data validation, analytical basis
  harmonization, engineered fuel-quality indices, cluster
  explainability via Random Forest feature importance, and a
  disagreement analysis comparing cluster-only,
  rule-only, and hybrid decision frameworks.
keywords:
  - bioenergy
  - waste-to-energy
  - biomass
  - thermochemical conversion
  - unsupervised clustering
  - decision support system
  - process suitability
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-09-18'